# Whole-development axiom audit (Phase 176)

*Created 21 October 2026. Last altered 31 October 2026 (repository check: the import list is
regenerated from the tree by `python3 -m glm_universal.lean_check --write-audit`; it now names the
Rule 30 files, and the files held in `src/lean/awaiting_recovery/` are left out until what they
import is recovered; `Wheels/CentWheels` was added to the list by hand in the sorted place, the
intake of `cent_compiler_v12`, directive D22).* Imports every Lean file of the development and
fails the build if any theorem in any of them depends on an axiom outside the standard set (`propext`,
`Classical.choice`, `Quot.sound`, `Lean.ofReduceBool`, `Lean.trustCompiler`, and the axioms
`native_decide`/`bv_decide` generate). An unfinished proof anywhere leaves `sorryAx` behind and fails it too.
This replaces reading `#print axioms` output by eye (the pipeline kit's `AxiomAudit.lean`) with a
check the build enforces. The import list must name every file; the test
`tests/test_axiom_guard.py` fails when a Lean file is missing from it.
-/

